# Relaxed from upstream's (>= 1.2.0-4.1). That floor is Debian's way of
# saying "must carry the fix for CVE-2026-111497", which 1.2.0-4.1 was a
# non-maintainer upload for. Ubuntu shipped the same patch in its own
# security updates instead -- 1.2.0-3ubuntu0.1 for resolute and
# 1.2.0-4ubuntu0.1 for stonking, both carrying debian/patches/
# CVE-2026-111497.patch -- and both sort BELOW 4.1, because a letter sorts
# before a dot in a dpkg version. So the literal floor is unsatisfiable on
# either target series while the fix is present on both. Verified in an
# ubuntu:26.10 container: the candidate is 1.2.0-4ubuntu0.1 from
# stonking-updates and stonking-security.
